  "scope": "Official September 21 signing announcement plus chaptered SB 1168 and AB 1577. The other five signed laws are identified but their operative text is not yet captured in this bounded packet.",
  "records": [
    {
      "sourceId": "governor-seven-law-signing-20260921",
      "title": "Governor Newsom signs most comprehensive data center laws in the nation",
      "url": "https://www.gov.ca.gov/2026/09/21/governor-newsom-signs-most-comprehensive-data-center-laws-in-the-nation-providing-communities-more-control-on-water-electricity-and-land-use/",
      "publisher": "Governor of California",
      "authority": "Official signing announcement; administration framing does not substitute for operative bill text",
      "raw": {
        "path": "operations/product-stewards/newsstand/candidates/california-data-centre-laws-20260921/source-refresh-20260926.json",
        "sha256": "e94266a8170e40100dac9e1489d4625debb04b67059ef1f23b38ce22b572cd92",
        "locator": "sources.0"
      },
      "exactPassages": [
        {
          "locator": "announcement overview",
          "excerpt": "Governor Newsom today signed seven bills to strengthen California’s approach to data centers — requiring data centers to report about water and electricity use."
        },
        {
          "locator": "signed-bill list",
          "excerpt": "AB 1577 by Assemblymember Rebecca Bauer-Kahan (D-Orinda). Data centers: reporting"
        },
        {
          "locator": "signed-bill list",
          "excerpt": "AB 2383 by Assemblymember Rick Chavez Zbur (D-Hollywood). Electricity: data centers."
        },
        {
          "locator": "signed-bill list",
          "excerpt": "AB 2469 by Assemblymember Diane Papan (D-San Mateo). Data centers: water use disclosures."
        },
        {
          "locator": "signed-bill list",
          "excerpt": "AB 2619 by Assemblymember Diane Papan (D-San Mateo). Water resources: data center."
        },
        {
          "locator": "signed-bill list",
          "excerpt": "SB 886 by Senator Steve Padilla (D-San Diego) and Senator Jerry McNerney (D-Pleasanton). California Technology Innovation and Ratepayer Protection Act."
        },
        {
          "locator": "signed-bill list",
          "excerpt": "SB 887 by Senator Steve Padilla (D-San Diego). California Environmental Quality Act: environmental leadership development projects: data centers: geothermal power plant projects."
        },
        {
          "locator": "signed-bill list",
          "excerpt": "SB 1168 by Senator Jerry McNerney (D-Pleasanton). Data centers: Rate structures."
        },
        {
          "locator": "electricity summary",
          "excerpt": "The new laws will also ensure data centers comply with California energy procurement requirements, bring new clean energy supply onto the grid, and pay for any upgrade costs. This legislation will prevent data centers from shifting costs onto everyday ratepayers."
        }
      ],
      "limitations": [
        "The page summarizes seven separate laws and uses promotional outcome language. Each claimed duty and outcome must be checked against the relevant chaptered text.",
        "The announcement does not establish an immediate reduction in any individual household bill."
      ]
    },
    {
      "sourceId": "sb1168-chaptered-20260921",
      "title": "SB 1168 — Data centers: rate structures",
      "url": "https://leginfo.legislature.ca.gov/faces/billNavClient.xhtml?bill_id=202520260SB1168",
      "publisher": "California Legislative Information",
      "authority": "Chaptered statutory text, Chapter 440",
      "raw": {
        "path": "operations/product-stewards/newsstand/candidates/california-data-centre-laws-20260921/source-refresh-20260926.json",
        "sha256": "e94266a8170e40100dac9e1489d4625debb04b67059ef1f23b38ce22b572cd92",
        "locator": "sources.1"
      },
      "exactPassages": [
        {
          "locator": "status",
          "excerpt": "Approved by Governor September 21, 2026. Filed with Secretary of State September 21, 2026."
        },
        {
          "locator": "Public Utilities Code section 901 opening",
          "excerpt": "As part of a new or existing proceeding, the commission shall assess opportunities for rate structures to do all of the following:"
        },
        {
          "locator": "section 901(a)",
          "excerpt": "Ensure data centers pay their reasonable share of costs associated with transmission and distribution needs, regardless of whether the data centers interconnect at the transmission or distribution level."
        },
        {
          "locator": "section 901(b)",
          "excerpt": "Ensure data centers pay for their proportionate share of load increases and procurements needed to reliably serve their loads while maintaining consistency with the applicable integrated resource planning requirements."
        },
        {
          "locator": "section 901(c)",
          "excerpt": "Alleviate cost pressures on residential ratepayers, including, but not limited to, customers enrolled in the California Alternate Rates for Energy program described in Section 739.1 and the Family Electric Rate Assistance program described in Section 739.12."
        }
      ],
      "limitations": [
        "The operative verb is assess opportunities within a commission proceeding. The statute does not itself select a rate structure, quantify savings, or guarantee a lower household bill.",
        "This packet does not identify a commission proceeding, implementation schedule, adopted tariff, utility-specific cost allocation, or customer-bill result."
      ]
    },
    {
      "sourceId": "ab1577-chaptered-20260921",
      "title": "AB 1577 — Data centers: reporting",
      "url": "https://leginfo.legislature.ca.gov/faces/billNavClient.xhtml?bill_id=202520260AB1577",
      "publisher": "California Legislative Information",
      "authority": "Chaptered statutory text, Chapter 434",
      "raw": {
        "path": "operations/product-stewards/newsstand/candidates/california-data-centre-laws-20260921/source-refresh-20260926.json",
        "sha256": "e94266a8170e40100dac9e1489d4625debb04b67059ef1f23b38ce22b572cd92",
        "locator": "sources.2"
      },
      "exactPassages": [
        {
          "locator": "status",
          "excerpt": "Approved by Governor September 21, 2026. Filed with Secretary of State September 21, 2026."
        },
        {
          "locator": "Government Code section 65909.3(a)",
          "excerpt": "Upon applying for a discretionary permit, entitlement, or land use authorization required for the construction or operation of a data center, the owner or operator of the data center shall submit to the applicable local agency an estimate of all of the following information, to the extent applicable to the proposed facility:"
        },
        {
          "locator": "Public Resources Code section 25302.10(a)(2)(B)",
          "excerpt": "“Data center” does not include a facility with an electrical capacity of less than 10 megawatts."
        },
        {
          "locator": "Public Resources Code section 25302.10(b)(1)",
          "excerpt": "The commission shall establish a process for the owner or operator of a data center to submit all of the following information to the commission upon energization of the data center and following any substantive change to information previously submitted pursuant to this paragraph:"
        },
        {
          "locator": "Public Resources Code section 25302.10(b)(2)",
          "excerpt": "The commission shall establish a process for the owner or operator of a data center to submit all of the following information to the commission at least annually following energization, disaggregated by month over the reporting period unless otherwise specified by the commission."
        },
        {
          "locator": "Public Resources Code section 25302.10(c)",
          "excerpt": "Beginning with the 2029 integrated energy policy report required pursuant to subdivision (a) of Section 25302, and in subsequent biennial reports required pursuant to subdivision (a) of Section 25302 thereafter as determined by the commission, the commission shall include an assessment of electrical load trends for data centers."
        },
        {
          "locator": "Public Resources Code section 25302.10(d)",
          "excerpt": "The commission shall annually publish the information submitted pursuant to subdivision (b) in an anonymized and aggregated format on its internet website."
        },
        {
          "locator": "Public Resources Code section 25302.10(f)",
          "excerpt": "This section does not apply to a publicly funded research facility, public safety facility, publicly funded national security facility, publicly owned facility, or other utility facility, including, but not limited to, a facility operated for the purpose of providing telecommunications services to the public by a terrestrial facilities-based telecommunications, cable, or internet service provider."
        },
        {
          "locator": "Government Code section 7927.303(a)",
          "excerpt": "The State Energy Resources Conservation and Development Commission or a local agency shall not disclose information submitted pursuant to Section 65909.3 of this code or to subdivision (b) of Section 25302.10 of the Public Resources Code in a manner that would result in the disclosure of personally identifiable information or energy consumption data for a specific data center customer."
        },
        {
          "locator": "Public Resources Code section 25302.10(e)(2)",
          "excerpt": "This subdivision does not require the disclosure of information that is exempted or prohibited from disclosure pursuant to the California Public Records Act (Division 10 (commencing with Section 7920.000) of Title 1 of the Government Code), or create an exemption from disclosure that does not otherwise exist under that act."
        }
      ],
      "limitations": [
        "The statute creates reporting processes and duties; it does not make every facility-level submission public. State publication is anonymized and aggregated.",
        "Facilities below 10 megawatts and the named public, safety, national-security and utility categories are outside these provisions.",
        "The commission specifies submission manner and timeframe; the statewide load-trend assessment begins with the 2029 integrated energy policy report."
      ]
    }
  ],
